  + [activation_profile] is cantor-environment-activation/0.1

& [SharedPreflight] is one core-owned admission gate
  + [implementation] is cantor_core environment module
  + [validation] is environment version, nonempty package set, semantic digest, every recognition certificate, trust admission, and complete SemanticFabric construction
  + [reuse] is cantor-mcp and cantord call the same preflight
  + [faults] are typed and bounded
  - never: let an adapter invent independent semantic readiness rules

& [ArtifactBoundary] is strict and operator-pinned
  + [configuration] is absolute strict JSON with loopback address, activation path, allowed environment root, token path, frame range, connection ceiling, and timeouts
  + [token] is exactly 64 hexadecimal characters loaded from a file and fixed-work compared
  + [activation] is a positive sequence, canonical root-contained environment path, exact file SHA-256, and canonical descriptor digest
  + [environment] is bounded to 64 MiB, strict JSON, fully preflighted, and converted to PreparedRuntime before use
  + [read_safety] is metadata size precheck plus a maximum-plus-one read and post-read growth check
  - never: accept request-selected artifact paths or unknown fields

& [ResidentRuntime] is immutable snapshot execution
  + [active_generation] is one Arc-backed PreparedRuntime and exact ActiveBinding behind a read-write lock
  + [execute] clones one complete generation before releasing the lock and returns the unchanged core ProtocolResponse
  + [refresh] loads the candidate outside the write lock then rechecks exact generation and activation sequence before a whole-generation swap
  + [failure] leaves the previous valid generation active
  + [rollback] is a previously valid environment published under a new higher sequence
  + [shutdown] requires the exact active generation and serializes against refresh
  - never: expose mixed old-and-new state or repair caller semantics

& [TransportImplementation] is explicit authenticated loopback TCP
  + [server] is cantord with one mandatory absolute configuration path
  + [client] is cantorctl with status, query, inspect, refresh, and shutdown commands
  + [framing] is one strict bounded JSON request plus LF and one bounded JSON response plus LF per connection
  + [resource_bounds] is 1024 through 1048576 frame bytes, 1 through 256 concurrent workers, and 1 through 60000 millisecond read and write timeouts
  + [overload] is visible connection-limit rejection after a bounded request drain when safely writable
  + [worker_lifecycle] is RAII connection accounting, joined worker handles, panic counting, and interrupted-accept retry
  + [shutdown_wake] is an explicit loopback wake connection rather than polling
  - never: bind non-loopback, expose the token, claim encryption, or claim hostile multi-user isolation

& [OperatorImplementation] is reproducible publication
  + [initializer] is scripts\initialize_cantor_service.ps1 with cryptographic 256-bit capability generation, containment precheck, atomic artifact writes, and explicit replacement
  + [publisher] is scripts\publish_cantor_activation.ps1 with increasing sequence enforcement, exact environment hash, and atomic descriptor replacement
  + [publication_order] is immutable environment first, activation descriptor second, authenticated compare-and-refresh third
  + [fallback] is direct cantor CLI and standalone cantor-mcp

